            {
                "entry_id": "b5257475-e84b-3ae6-b0c4-24cbdf4a993c",
                "word": "PUL",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c45205d8-ab31-3240-bc65-0eaa75688f68",
                        "entry_id": "b5257475-e84b-3ae6-b0c4-24cbdf4a993c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Abbreviation of polyurethane laminate (“a durable waterproof, machine-washable laminated fabric consisting of cloth and polyurethane”)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "179a1151-445e-42ee-b794-2fcf931346d8",
                                "sense_id": "c45205d8-ab31-3240-bc65-0eaa75688f68",
                                "text": "Today's options are much more comfortable to wear and touch. Cloth diaper covers can be polyurethane laminate (PUL) over cotton or polyester, nylon, wool or fleece."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b02cb062-425c-4a8b-a0a3-d606f53da5d3",
                                "sense_id": "c45205d8-ab31-3240-bc65-0eaa75688f68",
                                "text": "PUL is waterproof and yet can withstand the heat of the dryer, wool is breathable yet fairly waterproof and antimicrobial, hemp and bamboo are absorbent and have some antimicrobial properties."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc7e5904-1736-4340-9af6-8503cc8f9cab",
                                "sense_id": "c45205d8-ab31-3240-bc65-0eaa75688f68",
                                "text": "PUL is a slippery material and is not very easy to sew. Using a dual feed will simplify the sewing process. You can also use a Teflon presser foot, which reduces the slippery aspect. Alternatively, place a sheet of tracing paper between the PUL and the presser foot."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
